quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  26,1,"Ta, Sin, Mim."
  26,2,These are the Verses of the Manifest Book.
  26,3,(Esteemed Prophet!) You will perhaps consume yourself with grief that they are not becoming believers.
  26,4,"If We had wished, We could have sent down upon them a sign from the heavens at which their necks would remain bowed in utter humility."
  26,5,"There did not come to them any new reminder from the Most-Compassionate (Lord), except that they turned away from it."
  26,6,"They have indeed denied (the truth). So, the news of what they have been ridiculing will soon come to them."
  26,7,"Have they not looked at the earth, how much of every splendid kind of vegetation We have caused to grow in it?"
  26,8,"There is a sign in that, but most of them are not believers."
  26,9,"Indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,10,"And (remember) when your Lord called out to Musa (Moses), (saying:) ‘Go to the wrongdoing people,"
  26,11,the people of Pharaoh. Will they not become God-conscious?’
  26,12,"He (Moses) said: ‘My Lord! I fear that they will reject me,"
  26,13,"my breast will constrict (from the stress), and my tongue will not express (itself) fluently. Therefore, send (Your Messenger Gabriel) to Harun ([Aaron] to make him my helper)."
  26,14,"They also have a charge against me, and I fear they may kill me.’"
  26,15,"He (Allah) said: ‘No (they will not). Go, both of you, with Our signs. We shall be with you, listening (to everything)."
  26,16,So both of you approach Pharaoh and say: ‘We are indeed messengers of the Lord of the worlds.
  26,17,(We are commanded to say:) ‘Send with us the Children of Israel.’’
  26,18,"He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Did we not raise you among us as a child, and did you not stay several years of your life in our care?"
  26,19,"Then you did the act of yours which you did, and you are one of the ungrateful.’"
